remotix-install — the REMOTIX installation engine

One program: it installs, checks, certifies and uninstalls REMOTIX. It carries the CATALOG of the
supported combinations inside it, and the catalog is updated with this package
(`remotix-install catalog` shows it).

Updates
  REMOTIX is updated with the system, like any other program on the machine:
      apt upgrade · dnf upgrade · zypper up · pacman -Syu
  (or with the distribution's automatic updates, if the administrator turned them on).
  The service restarts without closing the desktops; then the package scripts run
  `remotix-install post-upgrade`, which records the versions and says whether the installation is
  still certified. No timer, no REMOTIX update system.

Going back to an earlier version: the package manager commands (the archive keeps the old versions):
      apt install remotix=VERSION remotix-install=VERSION    (the versions: apt list -a remotix)
      dnf downgrade remotix remotix-install
      zypper install --oldpackage remotix-VERSION remotix-install-VERSION
      pacman -U /var/cache/pacman/pkg/remotix-VERSION-x86_64.pkg.tar.zst
  then `remotix-install certify`.

Trust: one key only, the one that signs the REMOTIX packages and archive; the package manager
verifies it. install.sh is verified with the sha256 published on the REMOTIX site.
